      "text": "The IIP3 is plotted versus the value of V −V GS T for different CMOS technologies. It is clear that the higher the V −V , the higher the GS T IIP3 is but in a nonlinear way. It is also clear that for a V −V of 0.5 V, 15 dBm GS T IIP3 is readily available, independently of the technology. At V −V of 0.2 V, the GS T older CMOS technology provides the best IIP3. This is a result of the ever stronger effect of velocity saturation (parameter H) in deeper submicron technologies."
